Add `#` when a value must be known during compilation.

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    site_name #= "Moth"
    version #Int = 1
]

Constants cannot change.

They can be used by other compile-time values:

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    full_name #= [: [site_name] v[version]]
]

Use a normal binding when the value belongs to runtime code.

The initializer exception below belongs to accepted queued `$config` design; current
Alpha input contracts still use `#Config of T`.

Ordinary constants always need an initializer. A marked `$config` input may omit one;
required non-optional inputs then report missing input and optional inputs resolve to
absence. See @../../project-structure/#build-inputs (Build configuration values).
